metadata.rs:1216-1222:

  let args = json!({
      "accountId": "acc1",
      "filter": {
          "relatedIds": ["EM1", "EM2"]
          // relatedType deliberately omitted
      }
  });

The docstring at line 1213 describes relatedType: null. The test fixture omits the field. These are deserialize-equivalent (Option<T> with skip_serializing_if treats null and missing as both → None), but a contributor reading the docstring will look for an explicit null and not find it.

What would make it clear: docstring says 'with relatedIds: [...] and relatedType absent (or null — both deserialize to None per Option<String> default)'.
